// The ways an element gets into a list, or a value into a field: `push(xs, v)`,
// `xs[i] = v`, `t.f = v` and a list literal. A list of lists owns the element
// only when it is a list literal, which is a block nothing else holds yet;
// anything else -- a name, a call's result -- may be held by someone else
// already. A list of strings, a list of structs and a struct are freed by their
// type, all the way down, so what goes into them must be a string or a struct
// that nothing else holds, with the same held of whatever it holds (esc_ownv).
// Anything with nothing to free (an int, a float) is always fine. Flag bit 8.

esc_pushel(int[] args, string cname, string nm) {
  int r = 0;
  if(cname == "push") {
    r = esc_elbad(args[0], args[1], nm);
  }
} return int r;
